<p>India&#x27;s Lok Sabha failed to pass a constitutional amendment linked to the Modi government&#x27;s plan to reserve one-third of seats for women lawmakers while also redrawing parliamentary constituencies and expanding the size of the lower house. Opposition parties challenged the package because it tied the women&#x27;s reservation measure to delimitation, arguing the government had bundled a long-sought representation reform with an electoral boundary overhaul that could reshape political power. For now, that leaves the proposed quota, Lok Sabha expansion, and constituency redraw on hold, so neither women&#x27;s representation nor the current parliamentary map changes immediately. The result also shows that the government could not turn its majority into the broader support needed for a constitutional change affecting the electoral system.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/P9wTme4N27Zln4b7vsQZgCXpSHZr2pW3qcoVYARD9Iib3H3bFUJzufrH23TbvgUe8XfyHR35TU_PU2EwA0bJSSlDpz5zGZR6mSMfBXsDn576B29YhTUVUX-GbfdEyS-WdRdc5fFmI_nymw44pgj8LohSXzy_--yufnMU1xK6yQ' alt='India&#x27;s Parliament as lawmakers debated a constitutional amendment on women&#x27;s reservation and delimitation.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Constitutional math: Because this was a constitutional amendment, the bill needed more than a simple majority, which made opposition unity far more important than it would be on ordinary legislation.</li><li>Chamber size: DW reported that the package would have added hundreds of seats to the Lok Sabha, making this fight partly about how large the lower house should become.</li><li>Package framing: The Hindu described the amendment as part of a broader delimitation package, highlighting that MPs were voting on a wider restructuring plan, not just a quota bill.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Modi government: The government put forward the proposal as a single amendment rather than standalone quota legislation, signaling that it saw women&#x27;s reservation as tied to a broader reshaping of parliamentary representation. (<a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/india-parliament-blocks-modis-bid-redraw-voting-boundaries-132139703'>ABC News</a>, <a href='https://www.dw.com/en/india-modi-plan-for-women-s-quota-in-parliament-fails-vote/a-76818089'>DW</a>)</li><li>Opposition parties: Opposition lawmakers argued that tying the quota to delimitation could shift influence in ways that favored the BJP, turning support for women&#x27;s representation into a vote on electoral advantage. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/17/india-narendra-modi-women-representation-delimitationl'>The Guardian</a>, <a href='https://www.dw.com/en/india-modi-plan-for-women-s-quota-in-parliament-fails-vote/a-76818089'>DW</a>)</li><li>Parliament watchers: The vote showed that a governing majority does not guarantee success on constitutional questions, especially when changes to the electoral map draw resistance across party lines. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/17/india-narendra-modi-women-representation-delimitationl'>The Guardian</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/india-parliament-blocks-modis-bid-redraw-voting-boundaries-132139703'>India Parliament blocks Modi’s bid to redraw voting boundaries alongside seat quota for women</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/17/india-narendra-modi-women-representation-delimitationl'>India fails to pass bill to boost women’s representation after delimitation row</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/videos/watch-constitution-amendment-bill-part-of-delimitation-package-defeated/article70875160.ece'>Watch: Constitution Amendment Bill, part of delimitation package, defeated</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/india-modi-plan-for-women-s-quota-in-parliament-fails-vote/a-76818089'>India: Modi plan for women&#x27;s quota in parliament fails vote</a> - dw.com</li></ul>